You can check it out.
你可以检查一下。

00:43:51.969 --> 00:43:53.570
There's so many questions about this pilot.
关于这个飞行员有很多问题。

00:43:53.570 --> 00:43:57.289
There's 300 more here on Instagram and everywhere.
Instagram 上和其他地方还有 300 多个。

00:43:57.289 --> 00:43:58.289
Is there anything left?
还有东西吗？

00:43:58.289 --> 00:44:00.329
What else should we talk about about the pilot?
关于飞行员我们还应该谈论什么？

00:44:00.329 --> 00:44:02.289
Because we're moving on to episode two.
因为我们要继续看第二集。

00:44:02.289 --> 00:44:09.874
I would just say that one thing that struck me watching the pilot was the sense memory of challenge of having to have Robin meet the rest of the gang.
我只想说，观看试播集时令我印象深刻的一件事是，必须让罗宾与其他团伙见面的挑战感记忆。

00:44:09.874 --> 00:44:12.958
Robin, Kobe Smolder's only has scenes with Josh in the pilot.
科比·斯莫尔德的《罗宾》在试播集中只有乔什的镜头。

00:44:12.958 --> 00:44:14.880
She never interacts with anybody else.
她从不与其他人交往。

00:44:14.880 --> 00:44:27.824
And I remember that feeling at the end of the pilot, like we better have a good episode too that shows how she kind of works her way into this group and befriends this group because that's a whole other sale we have to make of like, she's the fifth banana.
我记得试播集结束时的感觉，就像我们最好也有一个好的剧集，展示她如何融入这个群体并与这个群体成为朋友，因为这是我们必须做的另一件事，她是第五根香蕉。

00:44:27.824 --> 00:44:31.566
She's, you know, she's the, she's the fifth part of this five part puzzle.
她是，你知道，她是，她是这个五部分拼图的第五部分。

00:44:31.566 --> 00:44:38.291
And we had to sort of integrate her and show how everybody else kind of fell in love with her two, and I had that feeling in my body.
我们必须将她融入其中，并向其他人展示如何爱上她两个，我的身体里就有这种感觉。

00:44:38.291 --> 00:44:42.083
It's sort of re-experienced that we got to somehow thread the needle on it.
我们必须以某种方式把针穿在上面，这有点像是重新经历的。

00:44:42.083 --> 00:44:43.246
I got to make the sale.
我必须完成销售。

00:44:43.246 --> 00:44:51.437
I remember feeling that way when we had to write episode two and three, and that we're sort of showing her becoming part of that group, and yeah, it was just fun.
我记得当我们必须写第二集和第三集时有这种感觉，我们有点让她成为这个团体的一部分，是的，这很有趣。

00:44:51.437 --> 00:44:55.027
Remember that challenge, and we'll rewatch and talk about if we did it.
记住这个挑战，我们会重新观看并讨论我们是否做到了。

00:44:55.027 --> 00:44:55.785
I think we did.
我想我们做到了。

00:44:55.785 --> 00:44:57.050
I think we pulled it off.
我想我们成功了。

00:44:57.050 --> 00:44:58.271
I have two things.
我有两件事。

00:44:58.271 --> 00:45:05.125
One is if you watch the pilot of how I made your mother, the DNA for the entire show is in the pilot.
一是，如果你观看《我如何造就你的母亲》的试播集，就会发现整个节目的 DNA 都在试播集中。

00:45:05.125 --> 00:45:13.541
Yeah, like absolutely, the entire kind of structure and essence and surprise switcheroo kind of thing that they did so well.
是的，就像绝对一样，他们做得很好，整个结构和本质以及令人惊讶的转换之类的事情。

00:45:13.541 --> 00:45:15.170
It's all, it's in there.
一切都在里面了。

00:45:15.170 --> 00:45:17.350
It's like the ragu sauce or whatever.
就像拉古酱什么的。

00:45:17.350 --> 00:45:18.764
It's like it's in there.
就好像它就在那里一样。

00:45:18.764 --> 00:45:22.241
What people understand that you can cut that if they don't.
人们理解的内容，如果他们不理解，你可以削减它。

00:45:22.241 --> 00:45:36.619
The other thing I wanted to say, this is just a funny anything that my wife said this morning, she was like, she knew someone who had who lived on the upper west side and he had a dog named Teddy and everyone called him the dog Teddy West side.
我想说的另一件事是，这只是我妻子今天早上说的一件有趣的事情，她就像，她认识一个住在上西区的人，他有一只名叫泰迪的狗，每个人都称他为狗泰迪西区。

00:45:36.619 --> 00:45:39.802
And I love, as one of Ted's, he had so many nicknames.
作为特德的一员，我喜欢他有这么多的绰号。

00:45:39.802 --> 00:45:41.864
Teddy West side's a great nickname.
泰迪西区是一个很棒的绰号。

00:45:41.864 --> 00:45:44.811
I thought, but it was also self proclaimed, right?
我想，但这也是自称吧？

00:45:44.811 --> 00:45:46.519
He called himself Teddy West.
他称自己为泰迪·韦斯特。

00:45:46.519 --> 00:45:49.515
Yeah, I think it's trying to get everyone else on board.
是的，我认为它正在努力让其他人都加入进来。

00:45:49.515 --> 00:45:50.692
They weren't on board.
他们不在船上。

00:45:50.692 --> 00:45:51.192
Yeah.
是的。

00:45:50.960 --> 00:45:52.227
She said, so where'd they live?
她说，那他们住在哪里？

00:45:52.227 --> 00:45:54.639
And I said, they, they lives on the Upper West side, right?
我说，他们，他们住在上西区，对吧？

00:45:54.639 --> 00:45:55.139
Yeah.
是的。

00:45:55.139 --> 00:45:55.639
Yeah.
是的。

00:45:55.639 --> 00:45:58.002
And she said, but Robin lives in Brooklyn.
她说，但罗宾住在布鲁克林。

00:45:58.002 --> 00:45:58.958
And I said, yeah.
我说，是的。

00:45:58.958 --> 00:46:07.957
And she said, because Robin's cool, because we, like, Jordan, she grew up in Manhattan, but she lives in Brooklyn and she just can't stand going into Manhattan.
她说，因为罗宾很酷，因为我们，就像乔丹一样，她在曼哈顿长大，但她住在布鲁克林，她就是无法忍受去曼哈顿。

00:46:07.957 --> 00:46:09.025
She loves Brooklyn.
她爱布鲁克林。

00:46:09.025 --> 00:46:14.987
But she said, how was she hanging out on this bar on the Upper West side so much if she lived in Brooklyn?
但她说，如果她住在布鲁克林，怎么会经常去上西区的这个酒吧呢？

00:46:14.987 --> 00:46:15.718
All the time.
一直以来。

00:46:15.718 --> 00:46:17.237
Yeah, It's a shady commute.
是的，这是一个阴暗的通勤。

00:46:16.800 --> 00:46:17.800
She would never.
她永远不会。

00:46:17.800 --> 00:46:18.800
Oh, that's terrible.
哦，那太可怕了。

00:46:18.800 --> 00:46:20.519
Here's what I rationalized.
这是我合理化的。

00:46:20.519 --> 00:46:22.840
I think her TV station is close by.
我想她的电视台就在附近。

00:46:22.840 --> 00:46:23.760
Yeah, let's say that.
是的，我们这么说吧。

00:46:23.760 --> 00:46:26.079
TV stations in Midtown somewhere.
市中心某处的电视台。

00:46:26.079 --> 00:46:26.920
So she's like, why not?
所以她想，为什么不呢？

00:46:26.920 --> 00:46:28.800
Or even in the West 60s.
甚至在西方60年代也是如此。

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:29.800
Like where in the DCs?
比如DC的哪里？

00:46:29.800 --> 00:46:34.440
Yes, the West 60s, like that sort of like CBS building, like West 50s, 60s, like that whole thing.
是的，西方 60 年代，就像 CBS 大楼那样，就像西方 50 年代、60 年代，就像整个事情一样。

00:46:34.440 --> 00:46:38.320
So then she just pops up a couple of like 10 or 15 blocks and hangs out with her friend.
于是她就突然出现在 10 或 15 个街区之外，和她的朋友一起出去玩。

00:46:38.320 --> 00:46:43.559
But also, she's out so late and she has to get up at like 3.30 in the morning to do the early.
而且，她出门这么晚，必须在凌晨 3.30 左右起床才能早起。

00:46:43.559 --> 00:46:44.880
Just to take like an hour and a half.
只需要一个半小时左右。

00:46:44.880 --> 00:46:47.159
These are the kind of threads we'll be pulling, that'll be.
这些就是我们将要拉动的线索。

00:46:47.159 --> 00:46:49.679
Yeah, at some point she moves, but it's true.
是的，在某些时候她会移动，但这是事实。

00:46:49.679 --> 00:46:52.079
For a while she had a real shit commute.
有一段时间，她的通勤经历真是糟糕透了。

00:46:52.079 --> 00:46:54.500
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:46:54.500 --> 00:46:56.380
Please equip me.
请装备我。

00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:58.699
Olsen's off again.
奥尔森又下课了

00:46:58.699 --> 00:47:01.139
New York City.
纽约市。

